Package: permeability
Title: Quantifying Permeability of Barriers for Animal Movement
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nicole", "Barbour", email = "nbarbour@towson.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Eliezer", "Gurarie", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates the permeability of a linear barrier from animal
    tracking data, with the option to model permeability as a function of
    covariates. Includes functions to format data, build a 'crossing table'
    of null and actual crossings of a barrier, plot crossings, and fit null
    and covariate models for model comparison and estimation of permeability. 
    For method details, see <doi:10.1111/2041-210x.70339>.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/NickiBarbour/permeability
BugReports: https://github.com/NickiBarbour/permeability/issues
LazyData: true
Encoding: UTF-8
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: sf, circular, MASS, dplyr, mgcv, ggplot2, ggspatial, plyr, parallel
Suggests: knitr, rmarkdown, future, future.apply, mapview, basemaps,
    viridis, lubridate, prettymapr
